What is HPA?

HPA (Horizontal Pod Autoscaler) automatically increases or decreases the number of Pods based on CPU, memory, or custom metrics.

Why Do We Need HPA?

Imagine your application has:

Morning: 100 Users
Afternoon: 500 Users
Night: 10,000 Users

If Deployment has:

replicas: 2

then only 2 Pods will always run.

Problem:

Traffic ↑
CPU ↑
Response Time ↑
Application Slow
Solution: HPA

HPA continuously monitors metrics.

CPU Usage ↑
      ↓
HPA Detects
      ↓
More Pods Created

Example:

1 Pod
  ↓
3 Pods
  ↓
5 Pods

automatically.

$kubectl autoscale deployment cpu-demo --cpu-percent=50 --min=1 --max=5
$kubectl get hpa
